<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    The Hemophage's shoulder pads, on VFEP's shoulder pad base (VFEP v4.03,
    1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Misc/Apparel_Various.xml). Plating, the research gate, the apparel
    tags, the text's shape and the masked tint follow the armor's header
    (Warcasket_Hemophage.xml).

    Tuning: the tier's baseline with the armor's Heat 1.5, as its header argues. Mass 20,
    insulation 22 / 22, SlaveSuppressionOffset 0.2 and VacuumResistance 0.1 are the same on
    all five of VFEP's spacer sets; Plasteel 60 is four of the five's price, about 0.4 of
    the armor's as across the tier. ComponentSpacer 2 pays for the pads' module, the
    Controller shoulders' price for theirs, and ComponentIndustrial 2 is the pool's first
    fill, since a crafted piece starts full. DevilstrandCloth 25 is the heat plating's price
    (the armor's header). There is no offset beyond those two.

    Dismember: the pads' module, an ability granted by the CompAbilitiesApparel below
    (AbilityDefs/Dismember.xml has it), limited by the strikes loaded in the reloadable
    beside it, which the ability reads off the piece that grants it. compClass CompStrikePool
    is vanilla's CompApparelReloadable kept within a capacity the settings can lower.
    - maxCharges 2 is vanilla's count for a strong single-target effect (both psychic
      lances): two strikes on one human leave 0.75 pain from the stumps alone, and one each
      cripples two.
    - ammoDef ComponentIndustrial, ammoCountPerCharge 1: a strike burns out a servo, and a
      component is 32 silver, inside the 23 to 92 a charge of vanilla's refillable packs
      costs and far under a lance charge's 275. Per-charge mode, so every empty slot is
      refilled by one item and a reload never discards any (vanilla's NeedsReload and
      ReloadFrom, 1.6).
    - baseReloadTicks 60 and soundReload are the family's. chargeNoun "strike" is what the
      stat sheet and the empty button count in.
    No verbs, so the comp draws no gizmo of its own; the ability's command shows the count.
    A colonist reloads on their own when undrafted, and a drafted pilot when ordered onto the
    components (vanilla's float menu). maxCharges and ammoCountPerCharge are mod settings.

    Art: the north facing is the south facing's silhouette shaded for the back, so the two
    share one mask and one glow sprite, shipped under both names because Graphic_Multi
    resolves each facing by its own file.

    Draw order: drawData's south offset 0.014 puts the pads under the helmet facing south, as
    the art wants the helmet's sides over the pauldron edges. A worn piece's altitude
    is its drawData offset y plus 0.000366 per render layer (ApparelBody 20, ApparelHead 70,
    plus the piece's index under that parent), so the base's 0.02 lands at about 0.028, just
    over the helmets' 0.027, and 0.014 at about 0.022, under any helmet and still over the
    shell's 0.018. Only this piece moves, so VFEP's helmets and armors mix with it as with
    each other. The other facings inherit the base's offsets, since inheritance merges
    drawData facing by facing, and the glow node takes its offset from the worn sprite, so
    the vials' glow goes under the helmet with the pads.

    ApparelExtension priority 1, for the reason in the armor's header; Merge still ORs the
    base's isUnifiedApparel in. Any new ApparelExtension field for the pads goes on this
    entry.

    Patched by the 1.6/Mods/CombatExtended/Patches/ root alone (plating on CE's scale, bulk,
    cost). 1.6/Patches/SOS2Patch.xml and the VGE vacuum patch leave shoulder pads alone, as
    VFEP's and VGE1's own patches do for VFEP's.
  -->
  <VFEPirates.WarcasketDef ParentName="VFEP_WarcasketShoulderPadBase">
    <defName>HPWC_WarcasketShoulders_Hemophage</defName>
    <label>hemophage warcasket shoulders</label>
    <shortDescription>Specialized spacer-tech warcasket pauldrons with improved heat protection, equipped with siphon vials that drain hemogen from the wound after the pilot tears a limb off an enemy.</shortDescription>
    <description>Specialized spacer-tech warcasket pauldrons with improved heat protection, equipped with siphon vials that drain hemogen from the wound after the pilot tears a limb off an enemy.\n\n10th generation warcaskets were adapted from captured pirate rigs by government military research divisions, who improved them with advanced power armor designs. The Hemophage series appears in none of their records. Some believe it was commissioned in secret by sanguophages who had worked their way into the program, so that those who already don't age or die naturally would be even harder to destroy.\n\nThe Hemophage series is built around the hemogen in its pilot's blood. Injectors in the shell can flood the pilot's body with it, which makes them much faster and stronger for as long as their hemogen lasts. Siphon vials on the pauldrons win some of it back from an enemy whose limb the pilot has torn away, and the sealed helmet keeps sunlight off the pilot's skin. Because all of this depends on hemogen, this series offers little to a pilot without any, but it suits a sanguophage who prefers to fight up close.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketHemophage/WarcasketHemophageShoulders</texPath>
      <shaderType>CutoutComplex</shaderType>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <Mass>20</Mass>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>2</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>1</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>1.5</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <Insulation_Cold>22</Insulation_Cold>
      <Insulation_Heat>22</Insulation_Heat>
      <EquipDelay>1</EquipDelay>
    </statBases>
    <equippedStatOffsets>
      <SlaveSuppressionOffset MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">0.2</SlaveSuppressionOffset>
      <VacuumResistance MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">0.1</VacuumResistance>
    </equippedStatOffsets>
    <costList>
      <ComponentSpacer>2</ComponentSpacer>
      <Plasteel>60</Plasteel>
      <ComponentIndustrial>2</ComponentIndustrial>
      <DevilstrandCloth>25</DevilstrandCloth>
    </costList>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>VFEP_SpacerWarcaskets</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_ApparelReloadable">
        <compClass>HemophageWarcasket.CompStrikePool</compClass>
        <maxCharges>2</maxCharges>
        <ammoDef>ComponentIndustrial</ammoDef>
        <ammoCountPerCharge>1</ammoCountPerCharge>
        <baseReloadTicks>60</baseReloadTicks>
        <soundReload>Standard_Reload</soundReload>
        <chargeNoun>strike</chargeNoun>
      </li>
      <li Class="VEF.Abilities.CompProperties_AbilitiesApparel">
        <abilities>
          <li>HPWC_Dismember</li>
        </abilities>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <apparel>
      <bodyPartGroups>
        <li>Shoulders</li>
        <li>Arms</li>
        <li>Hands</li>
        <li>Neck</li>
      </bodyPartGroups>
      <wornGraphicPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketHemophage/WarcasketHemophageShoulders</wornGraphicPath>
      <useWornGraphicMask>true</useWornGraphicMask>
      <!-- Under the helmet facing south; see "Draw order" in the header. -->
      <drawData>
        <dataSouth><offset>(0, 0.014, 0)</offset></dataSouth>
      </drawData>
      <renderNodeProperties>
        <li>
          <debugLabel>HPWC_HemogenGlow</debugLabel>
          <nodeClass>HemophageWarcasket.PawnRenderNode_HemogenGlow</nodeClass>
          <workerClass>HemophageWarcasket.PawnRenderNodeWorker_HemogenGlow</workerClass>
          <parentTagDef>ApparelBody</parentTagDef>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketHemophage/WarcasketHemophageShouldersGlow</texPath>
          <shaderTypeDef>TransparentPostLight</shaderTypeDef>
          <color>(1, 0.2, 0.15)</color>
        </li>
      </renderNodeProperties>
      <layers>
        <li>OnSkin</li>
        <li>Middle</li>
        <li>Shell</li>
      </layers>
      <tags>
        <li>WarcasketVeteran</li>
        <li>WarcasketAll</li>
      </tags>
    </apparel>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VEF.Apparels.ApparelExtension">
        <priority>1</priority>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VFEPirates.WarcasketDef>
</Defs>
